			"Message": "style(Mountain): Normalize emoji spacing in README.md badges and body text\n\nRemove the &#x2001; (em-space) Unicode separator after emoji characters and image badges across the README.md to eliminate inconsistent adjacent spacing in rendered output.\n\nThe previous commit introduced &#x2001; entities after every emoji and badge icon, resulting in visually uneven whitespace — particularly noticeable between Rust/Tauri SVG icons and their adjacent shields.io badges, and between emoji glyphs and inline code references throughout the Overview, Key Features, Architecture, and In the Land Project sections.\n\nAll 15 affected locations now render with natural spacing. Badge rows align cleanly and inline emoji no longer produce double-width gaps.",
			"SHA": "326bb572ed2dacf1b79205eec9e933d95e397ace"
		},
