				5
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Normalize Unicode thin spaces, update Rust version, and add Shim/ component references\n\nReplace literal emoji-space sequences (emoji + \\u{2001}) across all Markdown documentation with the canonical HTML entity `&#x2001;` for consistent rendering on GitHub and npm registries. Flatten multi-line table cells into single lines in README.md, DeepDive.md, and NamingConventions.md to reduce visual noise.\n\nUpdate the Rust version badge from 1.77+ to 1.95+, add the new `Shim/` module entry in the directory tree and component table for the VS Code engine deep-hook interception layer, and append License, Changelog, and Project Maintainers sections to README.md.\n\nAll documentation now uses consistent Unicode entities and reflects the current Rust edition-2024 baseline.",
			"SHA": "c2795322eacda270900442308fd8e10d00918ef2"
		},
